<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#142d4c"><meta name="description" content="Explore assistance programs available in Missouri."><title>Missouri Assistance Programs — American Aid Network</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/site.css"><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/google-analytics.php"; ?></head><body><?php require __DIR__ . "/../../includes/site-header.php"; ?><main><section class="state-page"><div class="wrap"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span>›</span><a href="/help/">Browse Programs</a><span>›</span><b>Missouri</b></div><div class="state-intro"><div><h1>Assistance Programs in Missouri</h1><p>10 programs, grouped by what you need help with. Each includes clear application guidance.</p></div><div><a class="button primary" href="/find/">Find my programs <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><small>Free · Private · Takes under 2 minutes</small></div></div><section class="program-group"><h2>Rent &amp; Housing Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>MO HealthNet (Missouri Medicaid)</h3><p>MO HealthNet is Missouri&#39;s Medicaid program: free or low-cost health coverage for children, pregnant people, parents, older adults, people with disabilities, and low-income adults. Missouri expanded Medicaid, so adults ages 19 to 64 can now qualify. Apply online at mydss.mo.gov or by phone at 1-855-373-9994. General MO HealthNet questions go to 1-800-392-2161.</p><div><a href="/programs/mo-healthnet-missouri-medicaid/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/mo-healthnet-missouri-medicaid/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Missouri Legal Aid (Free Civil Legal Help)</h3><p>Missouri&#39;s legal aid offices provide free civil legal help to low-income residents on housing, family, public benefits, consumer, and other noncriminal matters. In eastern Missouri, call Legal Services of Eastern Missouri at 1-800-444-0514. In western Missouri, call Legal Aid of Western Missouri at 1-816-474-6750. Find the right office and apply at lsmo.org.</p><div><a href="/programs/missouri-legal-aid-free-civil-legal-help/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/missouri-legal-aid-free-civil-legal-help/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>United Way 211 Missouri</h3><p>Dial 2-1-1 from any Missouri phone, or call 1-800-427-4626, for free, confidential help finding local assistance with housing, utilities, food, healthcare, and more. United Way 211 answers around the clock, every day of the year, with multilingual specialists. You can also search the statewide resource directory at 211helps.org.</p><div><a href="/programs/united-way-211-missouri/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/united-way-211-missouri/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Utility Bill Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Missouri Energy Assistance (LIHEAP &amp; ECIP)</h3><p>Missouri&#39;s Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program helps low-income households pay home energy bills. It has two parts: Energy Assistance, a one-time payment toward heating or cooling from October through May, and the Energy Crisis Intervention Program, ECIP, for a disconnect notice or an emergency. Apply at mydss.mo.gov or call 1-855-373-4636 to have an application mailed.</p><div><a href="/programs/missouri-energy-assistance-liheap-and-ecip/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/missouri-energy-assistance-liheap-and-ecip/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Weatherization Assistance Program (Missouri)</h3><p>Free home energy-efficiency work for income-eligible Missouri households: insulation, air sealing, and heating-system improvements that lower future bills. The Missouri Department of Natural Resources runs the program through a statewide network of local weatherization agencies. Contact the local agency serving your area to apply, since DNR does not take applications directly.</p><div><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-missouri/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/weatherization-assistance-program-missouri/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Food Assistance</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Missouri SNAP (Food Stamps)</h3><p>SNAP is Missouri&#39;s food stamp program: monthly food money on an EBT card you use like a debit card at most grocery stores. Apply online any time through myDSS at mydss.mo.gov, run by the Family Support Division, or ask for a paper application. The FSD Information Center is 1-855-373-4636 (1-855-FSD-INFO), Monday through Friday, 8am to 5pm.</p><div><a href="/programs/missouri-snap-food-stamps/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/missouri-snap-food-stamps/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Missouri WIC</h3><p>WIC gives healthy food, breastfeeding support, nutrition education, and health referrals to pregnant and postpartum people, infants, and children up to age 5. Missouri WIC runs through local agencies of the Department of Health and Senior Services. Call TEL-LINK at 1-800-835-5465 to find your local WIC agency, or reach the state WIC office at 1-800-392-8209.</p><div><a href="/programs/missouri-wic/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/missouri-wic/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Cash Assistance &amp; Benefits</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Missouri Temporary Assistance (Cash Assistance)</h3><p>Temporary Assistance, TA, is Missouri&#39;s monthly cash benefit for low-income families with children, meant to help cover costs like clothing and utilities. Most adults take part in the Missouri Work Assistance program, which helps you move toward a job. Apply online at mydss.mo.gov or ask for a paper application through the FSD Information Center at 1-855-373-4636.</p><div><a href="/programs/missouri-temporary-assistance-cash-assistance/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/missouri-temporary-assistance-cash-assistance/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article><h3>Unemployment Insurance (Missouri)</h3><p>Temporary weekly payments if you lost work through no fault of your own, from the Missouri Division of Employment Security. File online through UInteract at uinteract.labor.mo.gov, which is the fastest way and open 24 hours a day, or call a Regional Claims Center at 1-800-320-2519, Monday through Friday, 8am to 5pm Central.</p><div><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-missouri/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/unemployment-insurance-missouri/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><a class="group-cta" href="/find/">Check what you qualify for <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></section><section class="program-group"><h2>Debt &amp; Credit Help</h2><div class="directory-cards"><article><h3>Missouri Working Family Tax Credit</h3><p>Missouri&#39;s Working Family Tax Credit is a state earned income tax credit equal to 20 percent of your federal Earned Income Tax Credit for tax year 2024 and forward. It is nonrefundable, so it lowers the Missouri tax you owe but cannot go below zero, and it cannot be carried forward to a later year. Claim it on your Missouri income tax return.</p><div><a href="/programs/missouri-working-family-tax-credit/">How to apply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a href="/programs/missouri-working-family-tax-credit/">Program details <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div></section></div></section></main><footer><div class="wrap footer-grid"><div><a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="American Aid Network home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><span>★</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>AMERICAN <b>AID</b><small>NETWORK</small></span></a><p>Clear, reliable guidance to assistance programs across America.</p><div class="verified">✓ Information from trusted sources</div></div><div><h4>FIND SUPPORT</h4><a href="/find/">Find help near me</a><a href="/help/">Browse by state</a><a href="/programs/">Program guides</a><a href="/#how-it-works">How it works</a></div><div><h4>ABOUT</h4><a href="/about/">Our mission</a><a href="/legal/contact/">Contact us</a><a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy policy</a><a href="/legal/terms/">Terms of use</a></div></div><div class="wrap disclaimer">American Aid Network is an independent informational resource. We are not a government agency and do not administer benefit programs. Program details change; always confirm requirements with the official provider.<span>© 2026 American Aid Network</span></div></footer><script src="/assets/site.js" defer></script></body></html>